# serializer version: 1
# name: test_runbook_snapshot
  '''
  # DNG Deployment Runbook

  > Auto-generated by dng-preflight. Review before executing.
  >
  > **Scope:** web_ssh
  > **IdP:** okta
  > **Public hostname:** `dng.example.com`
  > **DNG minimum version:** 3.3.0

  This runbook is ordered to resolve the SAML circular dependency: DNG needs the
  IdP's metadata to validate signatures, but the IdP needs DNG's SP metadata to
  know who is asking. We bring DNG up with a placeholder primary_auth, export
  SP metadata, configure the IdP, then return and complete primary_auth.

  ---

  ## Step 0 — DNS records

  Publish the records listed in `dns-records.md` **before** running the
  installer. The installer refuses to proceed unless `dng.example.com`
  resolves.


  ## Step 1 — Run the installer

  ```bash
  sudo ./install.sh
  ```

  The installer is idempotent. It will:

  1. Verify the host is not domain-joined.
  2. Verify `dng.example.com` resolves.
  3. Install Docker Engine + Compose plugin if missing.
  4. Place `scripted-config.yaml` at `/etc/dng/scripted-config.yaml`.
  5. Pull `duosecurity/network-gateway:3.3.0`.

  ## Step 2 — Apply firewall rules

  ```bash
  sudo ./firewall.sh
  ```

  This opens public port 443 and restricts admin port 8443 to internal CIDRs.

  ## Step 3 — Paste TLS material into scripted-config.yaml

  Open `/etc/dng/scripted-config.yaml` and replace the `<<paste contents of …>>`
  markers with the actual file bodies:

  - `network_gateway.ssl_cert.cert` ← contents of `/etc/ssl/dng/cert.pem`
  - `network_gateway.ssl_cert.key`  ← contents of `/etc/ssl/dng/key.pem`

  Set file perms to `0600` after editing.

  ## Step 4 — First-time DNG bring-up (placeholder primary_auth)

  The committed `scripted-config.yaml` ships with placeholder values for
  `primary_auth`. That is intentional — we need DNG running to export its SP
  metadata before the IdP can be configured.

  ```bash
  sudo docker run --rm \
      -v /etc/dng/scripted-config.yaml:/config/scripted-config.yaml:ro \
      duosecurity/network-gateway:3.3.0 \
      init
  sudo docker compose -f /etc/dng/docker-compose.yml up -d
  ```

  > Wait ~30 seconds for the container to become healthy.

  ## Step 5 — Export DNG SP metadata

  ```bash
  curl -fsSL https://dng.example.com/metadata/ \
      -o dng-sp-metadata.xml
  ```

  Hand `dng-sp-metadata.xml` to your IdP administrator.

  ## Step 6 — Configure the IdP

  In **Okta**, add a new SAML 2.0 application with:
  - Single sign-on URL: `https://dng.example.com/acs/`
  - Audience URI (SP Entity ID): `https://dng.example.com/metadata/`
  - Application username: Email

  After the IdP is configured, export its metadata (an XML file) and note:

  - IdP entity ID
  - IdP SSO URL
  - IdP signing certificate (PEM block from `<ds:X509Certificate>`)

  ## Step 7 — Import IdP metadata into DNG

  Open `/etc/dng/scripted-config.yaml` and fill in `primary_auth`:

  ```yaml
  primary_auth:
      entity_id: '<IdP entity ID from Step 6>'
      single_signon_url: '<IdP SSO URL from Step 6>'
      signing_cert: |
          -----BEGIN CERTIFICATE-----
          ...
          -----END CERTIFICATE-----
  ```

  Restart DNG:

  ```bash
  sudo docker compose -f /etc/dng/docker-compose.yml restart
  ```

  ## Step 8 — First-login password reset

  The placeholder `network_gateway.password` in `scripted-config.yaml` is for
  config-time use only. On first admin login at
  `https://dng.example.com:8443/`, DNG requires you to set a
  new password via shell access to the container:

  ```bash
  sudo docker exec -it dng /opt/dng/reset_admin_password
  ```

  ## Hard-stop summary

  The following rules were enforced before generating this runbook
  (`dng-preflight validate --plan plan.yaml`):

  - Host not domain-joined: ✓
  - Time offset within ±30s of NTP: ✓
  - Public hostname resolves on at least one authoritative resolver: ✓
  - DNG version ≥ 3.3.0: ✓

  ---

  _Generated by dng-preflight 0.1.0._

  '''
# ---
